  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two concentric circular loops of radii <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> are placed in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Y</mi></math> plane as shown in the figure. A current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is flowing through them in the direction as shown in figure. The net magnetic moment of this system of two circular loops is approximately</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0c325fed-1b88-4e62-9b5c-3d016bccadf2-image.png\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 122px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
